{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795818100,"nonce":"XS+xg0rC0voR6o0PqKWCoUncVMc=","title":"A padding or margin longhand in @keyframes animates the other sides to zero","message":"`@keyframes grow { to { padding-left: 20px; } }` also moves top, right and\nbottom to zero. CSS animates only the side a keyframe declares.\n`KeyframeProperties::padding` and `margin` hold all four sides, so the\nconversion from `ElementStyle` fills an undeclared side with zero. The values\nneed to be optional per side through interpolation and through the layout\napply step.","files":null}]}